// The catalogue of the host's creature library (2026-10-17, the host's words: "we should do the same thing for all
// creatures as well", as for places and people: ready-made pictures, so creatures stop costing paintings). Every kind
// of creature a tale in this game meets, in Questbound's own words (the SRD's licensed creatures and plain fantasy;
// never another publisher's creatures or names): beasts, monstrosities, the dead, fiends and fey in plain terms,
// giants and trolls, raiders as bands, dragons, drakes and wyverns, oozes, elementals, constructs, plants and fungus,
// tentacled horrors, swarms, deep and sea things, and armed outlaws, cultists and soldiers seen as a band.
// Each entry: id `kind-variant`, family, size, whether it shows a band, the lands it fits, `names` (the words that say
// what it is: matched first), `tags` (look and habitat words that tell one variant of a kind from another),
// `templates` (encounterRules.js templateKeys it can stand for), a painting description in our own words (`look`), and
// one or two variants (`twist`: what sets the second apart; `template`: the variant that IS that template's own look,
// whose painting already exists and is copied into the library free). A picture's id is the entry's id and its number
// (wolf-grey-1). make-creature-library.cjs paints each picture once; creature-library.cjs matches creatures to them.
// verify-creature-library.cjs checks the count, the ids, the words and that every template is covered.
const templateLooks={
 bandit:'A lean human bandit in a patched leather jerkin and a mud-stained hood, a notched scimitar in one hand and a knife in the other. A scarf covers the lower face; a crude tattoo of a crow marks one wrist.',
 wolf:'A huge grey-black wolf, ribs showing through matted fur, yellow eyes and a torn left ear. Its muzzle is scarred and its hackles stand high.',
 goblin:'A wiry green-grey goblin with oversized ears, a jagged grin and a helmet made from a dented cooking pot. It carries a chipped short blade and a rope belt hung with stolen trinkets.',
 skeleton:'A yellowed human skeleton in rusted mail scraps, a cracked round shield strapped to one arm and a corroded shortsword in hand. Faint blue light flickers in its eye sockets.',
 boar:'A massive bristle-backed boar with curved, chipped tusks, a torn ear and a broken arrow shaft lodged in its flank. It paws furrows into the earth.',
 spider:'A spider the size of a large dog, with glossy black legs banded in rust red, eight clustered amber eyes and dripping fangs. Web strands trail from its abdomen.',
 zombies:'A shambling corpse in the rags of a farmhand’s smock, grey skin split and sagging, one eye clouded white. Its jaw hangs loose and dirt cakes its reaching hands.',
 orc:'A broad-shouldered grey-green orc with a shaved scalp, jutting lower tusks and a scarred lip, wearing scavenged ring mail and a wolf-pelt mantle. It swings a heavy notched greataxe.',
 wolves:'A lean grey timber wolf with a pale chest, amber eyes and a ridge of raised fur along its back. Its lips pull back from long yellowed fangs.'
};
const all=['plains','forest','hills','mountains','coast','marsh','desert','snow','caverns'];
const families=['beast','monstrosity','undead','fiend','fey','giant','raider','folk','dragon','ooze','elemental','construct','plant','aberration','swarm'];
const sizes=['tiny','small','medium','large','huge','gargantuan'];
// e(id, family, size, band, lands, names, tags, templates, look, ...twists): the first picture is the look itself (or,
// when the first twist is T(template), that template's own look), then one picture for each further twist ({twist, tags}).
// `lands` may also name kinds of place where it is met (ruin, settlement, road...): kept apart as `places`; a
// creature that names no land fits every land.
const e=(id,family,size,band,lands,names,tags,templates,look,...variants)=>({id,family,size,band,terrains:lands.some(t=>all.includes(t))?lands.filter(t=>all.includes(t)):[...all],places:lands.filter(t=>!all.includes(t)),names,tags,templates,look,variants:(variants[0]?.template?variants:['',...variants]).map(v=>typeof v==='string'?{twist:v,tags:[]}:{tags:[],twist:'',...v})});
const T=(template,twist='',tags=[])=>({template,twist,tags});
